Z||000000||BlackStang95||11-27-2001||01:55 AM||||You guys came down way too hard on matt, although his post was a little offensive.  The late model (90+) z's were incredible cars, are almost as rare as a fiero (the twin turbos are even more rare), beautiful to look at, all kinds of great options available, aka abs, traction control, hicas (rear wheel steering) etc., handle very well, and are straight up incredibly fast.  Me and spek have driven our friends 90 twin turbo and the feeling when that boost kicks in is incredible.<P>1990   Nissan300ZX                           7.1            15.5<P>1990   Nissan 300ZX Turbo                     6.5            15.0<P>1990   Nissan 300ZX Twin Turbo                5.6            14.1<P><BR>As you can see, a stock fiero gt would barely have a chance against a non turbo one, and they got faster as the years went on.<BR>||||reg||1
