Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||11-27-2001||03:08 PM||||I have had several friends with 300ZX TT's Fast cars granted. But what good does it do to compare a Fiero to a 300ZX TT.. a wee bit of a price difference.<P>Both my friends had thier cars boosted to over 400hp. The car was never the problem , it's the weight , the motor alone weighs 600+ Lbs!!! My friend just did a rebuild on his and it was quite costly.<P>Great highway / touring car a wee bit too heavy for my tastes. 3500lbs ++ is a heavy car. Most guys that boost the HP remove the Super Hiacas 4 wheel steering ala Steve Millen.<P>Great cars , I have yet to ride in my friends 420hp car , but at the autocross he had no problems smoking the tires at any speed. The car is heavy though , for track events he installed a wiper motor in the trunk attached to a bottle of water. Under the brake pedal is a switch when it's armed it spray's water into the veins of the rotors to  cool the brakes.<P>I think the late 80's early 90's 240 is a better platform for perfomrance. The friend of mine that hadthe 300zx TT traded it and got a 240 , handles a lot better , he adapted the 300zx TT 4 piston calipers and rotors.. Just a more nimble "real" feeling sports car...No where near the power though.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
