Z||000032||Groove Champion||11-28-2001||03:20 PM||||I have been lurking on the Forum for a while , I have tried to stay out of a lot of the mustang / Fiero conversations.<P>Blackstang , It's nice to see you have a passion about a certian mark , but as someone who has raced mustangs since the early 70's (Longer than you have been alive no doubt) I can tell you your way out to lunch when you say a suspension upgrade on a mustang will make it handle better than  a Fiero.<P>The platform of the mustang just doesn't lend itself to optimum lateral G characteristics the way the Fiero does. The weight balance of a Fiero is far superior to a mustangs. Mustangs can be made to handle quite well , I raced in Showroom stock , Autocrossed in ESP (scca Events) and ran probably thousands of events in the last 30 years with a mustang. In The US and Canada<P>Mustangs lend themselves far better to drag racing than roadracing. A fiero is a more enjoyable car around a track than a mustang is. Mustangs "hobby Horse" quite a bit more than Fiero's and the suspension is your typical pony car design that no matter how modified will have a hard time competing with a Independently suspended car.<P>There are hundereds of references I could cite , but I don't think there is much point. I have a 5.0ltr right now , it's a fun car I use it as a daily driver and  sees some track use. I can tell you that stock for stock at Mosport the Fiero (87 GT 5spd) is faster by about 2 seconds. The mustang has more power , but not enough to overcome it's suspensions short comings.<P>I love my 5.0ltr to death .. I think v8 mustangs are one of the best performance bargians to come out of the last 20 years (c4 vette is probably better due to suspension , but i', partial to 5.0ltrs)<P>You can argue this all you would like , but keep in mind I have been racing them for longer than you have been alive. I have driven a few "setup" Fiero's (not even 88's) and none of the mustangs I have ever had (23 and counting) have ever come close to the go kart like handling a setup Fiero has. <P>It seems with some people on the Forum , and in the car world in general sit on a fine line between car guy who generally just loves all cars and ignorance , someone who thinks that their car is the ultimate ..no matter what. (corvette guys?)<P>My personal thoughts from years and years experience behind the wheel of  mustangs. The best handling mustang I had was an EX NYS police LX 5.0ltr setup for ESP SCCA use.  Fast fun car. I have only had the Fiero about 9 months now. <P>GC.<BR>87 GT stock..but not for long.<BR>95 5.0ltr 5spd , B&M ripper shifter , SVO side pipes.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000033||California Kid||11-28-2001||03:33 PM||||Great input Groove Champion, coming from one who has raced Mustangs on the track just might make someone a believer!<P>Good Luck on your project Fiero, you're going to have a great car when you're done! Attached a clip from C5Corvette, he raced for Porsche, bought the car from him about 5 years ago. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/C5_Note_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
