Z||000036||BlackStang95||11-29-2001||12:59 AM||||Groove you sound cool, and I agree with most everything you said, but its possible (and mind you i did say a complete suspension replacement) to put independent suspension in stangs.  That's what they did for the 00 cobra r, which pulled over a G on the pad and outperformed both a corvette z06 and viper gts on the track.  That's a hell of an accomplishment, starting from a 6 cylinder car like mine and not having the advantage of mid engine.<P>Jeffrey Sucko, if you think that's my attitude you need to brush up on your reading comprehension skills, I'm sorry if to your puny little mind it appears I'm saying my car can beat anything when I correct completely false statements on the forum.<p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||California Kid||11-29-2001||01:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Groove you sound cool, and I agree with most everything you said, but its possible (and mind you i did say a complete suspension replacement) to put independent suspension in stangs.  That's what they did for the 00 cobra r, which pulled over a G on the pad and outperformed both a corvette z06 and viper gts on the track.  That's a hell of an accomplishment, starting from a 6 cylinder car like mine and not having the advantage of mid engine.<BR>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-29-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>What the heck, my car will beat the ones you mentioned on a road coarse! You missed the point of weight distribution.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000038||Jefrysuko||11-29-2001||03:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Jeffrey Sucko, if you think that's my attitude you need to brush up on your reading comprehension skills, I'm sorry if to your puny little mind it appears I'm saying my car can beat anything when I correct completely false statements on the forum.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ha your funny.  I know this isn't worth it but to tell you the truth it is rather fun getting you stirred up.  Also I feel that you should know better than to make statements about someone's intellect when they clearly state that they are attending one of the leading educational institutions in this country.  So as in so many other cases, you asked for it.<P>First of all to emulate is not to make an exact copy.  To emulate is to make similar at best.  An emulation commonly surpasses what it is imitating.  So as you should be able to see, but obviously don't, in Slammed Fiero's emulation of your attitude he surpassed it by the statements you objected to.  Second of all without understanding what an emulation was you still should have been able to grasp the intent of Slammed Fiero's post by me explaining that it was SARCASM.  I know that you know how to use sarcasm for you do so on a regular basis.  It is now obvious that you do not comprehend it therefore you are in fact the one with the reading comprehension problems.  The funny thing is that I made the statement about sarcasm because I thought you would be able to understand it.<P>So as you can see, or should be able to see, nor to Slammed Fiero or myself does it appear that you are saying "my car can beat anything."  I stand by my statement that his emulation was a damn good one for if I had read his statement and not know who he was referring to, I would have immediately thought of you.<P>Now that you made statements about my intellect referencing what you perceived to be my lack of comprehension which, turned out to be false.  I believe that indicates you are the one of lesser intellect.  If you would like to challenge me again I would gladly accept but I would at least recommend you reference a dictionary.<P>Before you go running off crying about how I have been picking on you and stating how much smarter I am than everyone, the only person I said I was smarter than was you, and you weren't that much of a challenge.  I just wanted to make that clear because I know you have a little problem with your comprehension skills.<P>Lastly, this is the second time you have spelled my name like that and this is the only time I am going to say this.  Don't do it again!||||reg||1
Z||000039||artherd||11-29-2001||05:31 AM||||Yawn, my *t-top* car can turn inside a Cobra R. (It's actually HARD to make a Fiero not able to pull over a static Gee.)<P>PS: Friend of mine owns one. It's black. *Nice* friggin sweet motor! The independant rear end makes all the difference in the world too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Hopefully we'll see the demize of the live axel and pushrod motors, in favour of at least Cobra level 4.6 DOHC v8 (if not the crazy punched DOHC in the R)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Groove you sound cool, and I agree with most everything you said, but its possible (and mind you i did say a complete suspension replacement) to put independent suspension in stangs.  That's what they did for the 00 cobra r, which pulled over a G on the pad and outperformed both a corvette z06 and viper gts on the track.  That's a hell of an accomplishment, starting from a 6 cylinder car like mine and not having the advantage of mid engine.<P>Jeffrey Sucko, if you think that's my attitude you need to brush up on your reading comprehension skills, I'm sorry if to your puny little mind it appears I'm saying my car can beat anything when I correct completely false statements on the forum.<P>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-29-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000040||Groove Champion||11-29-2001||08:53 AM||||I drove a cobra R with the independent suspension probably before any of you even saw the carin a magazine. (In Arizona at the proving grounds, Techs were invited to test them out<P>Great car , handles really well , Better than a Z06?? well I don't know about that. Most road tests (if your a roadtest guy) have the vette being faster on the track. And in a straight line. I have lurked on the Vette forum  (I want a v8 swap in my fiero) and heard Stock Z06's turning 12.1's The best #'s I have ever seen from FoMoCo is 12.9's for the Cobra R. Even with it's independent rear suspension there are traction problems when launching the car. Also keep in mind that the vette has a rear mounted transaxle much like a 944 / 928 porsche. This helps the weight distribution greatly and gets it over the rear wheels where it is needed. <P>As for swapping in an independent suspension. I have seen it done using a T-Bird rear setup , but for the cost you may as well buy a car with the independent suspension. The whole rear pan (so to speak) has to be cut and strengthened. Mounting points have to be changed. Just  engineering nightmare , but it can be done.<P>Will it handle better than a Fiero... Good question , I think the weight distribution will still be a major factor in the way the car reacts to inputs. Plus the motor is still out front , and while your weight distribution may change a bit , you still run into problems. To put it in better terms The fastest cars in the world are mid engined for a reason<P>The great thing about a mid engined car is that you can Up the HP with having no real affect on the way the car handles. I'm not comparing Fiero's to F1's cars , But there are a lot of similar principles that translate over.  Weight changes under brakng and cornering for a mid engine cars are a lot less drastic than a front engined car car. <P>Anyone here know what a pantera is or driven one? a well setup Pantera is a ball to drive, about as close to a mid 70's Can Am Car as you can get. If you don't have one of those at your disposal try a Lotus Europa. Not much in the way of HP but such a fantasic car to drive.<P>Arthered, a Black Cobra R? I was sure they only made them in Red. Perhaps you mean a Cobra.<P>Also a factor to keep in mind is that every so called sports car today is in need of a diet. 3300lbs is FAT. Most people would agree with the fact that the Fiero is a bit overweight. (should be 2500lbs)<P>I hope this helps shed some light on all of these  isses you all seem to love to discuss. IF I were building a drag car it would be a mustang , if I wanted a Track car , regaurdless of what it was , the motor would be behind me.<P>As for breaking 1G. I suggest you find a roadtest on an 84 z51 Vette. When those came out they gave mustang drivers a fit on the track. Over 1 G in 1984. We really haven't come as far as we would like to think. Ride quality has gotten better , but overall handling #'s really haven't imporved greatly.<P>Lateral G's are a good gauge if your into racing in 300Ft circles (I believe someone else here said that) but when it comes to real world handiling and racing there's a whole lot more than that. Lateral G's are used to sell cars.<P><BR>GC<BR>87 GT. ||||reg||1
Z||000041||firstfiero||11-29-2001||10:14 AM||||      Are you sure its a cobra R. I went back and checked car and driver and they said it only comes in red.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000042||BlackStang95||11-29-2001||01:13 PM||||Cobra R's did come in only perfromance red in 2000.  Only white in 1995.  Good example of the incorrect facts about Mustangs spread all over this forum. The road test I was referring to was motortrends.  It was over 2 seconds faster than the vette or viper on the track, and only a couple tenths slower to 60 despite the traction problems.  <P>Jeffrey Sucko, just because you go to a decent school doesn't mean you have a damn bit of common sense.  I don't really care what you or jm think of me or my attitude, thats the beauty of it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
