Z||000045||Voytek||11-29-2001||02:36 PM||||In defense of BlackStang - I did see the comparison on the track in 2000 (if I remember correctly it was a yellow Vette with a red Stang and I think a red Viper).<BR>Yes, the Mustang was slightly faster than both, the viper and the Vette.  HOWEVER, I remember comments in the show, such as 'the car, in this form will never make it to the dealerships'.  It was FACTORY modded.  The Vette was all stock and so was the Viper.<P>This post isn't intended to excuse Stang95 from all other bull presented by him on the PFF.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>As for swapping in an independent suspension. I have seen it done using a T-Bird rear setup , but for the cost you may as well buy a car with the independent suspension. The whole rear pan (so to speak) has to be cut and strengthened. Mounting points have to be changed. Just engineering nightmare , but it can be done.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, exactly.  ANYTHING can be done with the right kind of cash.  Hell, I could make a '69 VW Van handle better than a Mustang for the right amount of money (you know, chop the whole top off, etc.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )  The point is, stock Fieros handle better than stock mustangs - no question about it.  That's the beauty of mid-engines.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
