Z||000048||Jefrysuko||11-29-2001||04:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>I care what some people on this forum think about me, that's why i take (waste) the time to correct you on your   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  statements.  You are not one of those people.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First of all you have yet to correct me on anything.  Second of all you have shown that you do care what I think about you and I have all but proved it in a court of law (see above).  So would you please stop blindly refuting the facts it only makes you look less and less competent.  Also when you continually show everyone that you are mentally incapable of comprehending anything I say it makes it look as if I am picking on you.  So for the sake of our argument please come up with a logical response for once.||||reg||1
Z||000049||RedHaze86SD4||11-29-2001||04:41 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Jus' stickin ma nose in here too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>I gotta say hey to Groove Champion, cuz' I used to work for two of the proving grounds down here in Texas. And oh what fun that is. And whats this about the stang only being sold in performance red for 2000 and the white for 95, BUT thats not, entirely correct. They were supposed to be the only colors offered. However, if you were ever at the track or around the S-team boys youd know that in reality they came in red, white, black and like 4 blue ones were made. Of course the blue ones don't count because they were hand picked by the S-team boys. (lucky SOB's) Yes I know, the "production numbers are for the colors you stated, but face it, there is a thing called special ordering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> One of the guys at the track has a 2000 R that was purchased NEW! solid black, after some mods he was hittin' 11.9's with slicks. I used to know two other guys that had R's also one was a white 2000 and the other was a black 95. <BR>Ok wel thats enough for now. ||||reg||1
